|-
! Period !! Wave !! Estimated arrivals !! Primary drivers
|-
| 1738–1747 || First Civil War refugees || ~2,000 || [[First Sartan Civil War]], baronial conflict, rural devastation
|-
| 1799–1811 || Second Civil War refugees || ~4,000 || [[Second Sartan Civil War]], mass displacement, Volisanian intervention
|-
| 1824 || Guajicutea-originated Sartans || ~1,000 || [[Virtuous Revolution]], displacement of Sartan privileged class from [[Guajicutea]]
|-
| 1811–1846 || Post-civil war exiles and displaced peasants || ~3,000 || Serfdom abolition (1838), political unrest, rural restructuring
|-
| 1854–1890 || Redilution and Birthing || ~16,000 || Government-sponsored immigration, land grants, economic opportunity
|-
| 1912–1947 || Authoritarian-era refugees and wartime migration || ~5,000 || Checa regime, political persecution, GAW famine and collapse
