The Redilution programme accounts for the majority of Sartan Balboan ancestors. The civil war and post-civil war waves were smaller in number but established the community's initial presence on the isthmus, while the authoritarian-era wave was culturally significant, bringing political dissidents and professional-class immigrants who diversified the community's social composition.

